        "id": 94397,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-04T00:03:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>When you get Necro going he is insanely good. &nbsp;That's why you have the cost of the zombie attacks.</p><p>My sister plays as him a lot, and by turn 5 she's either nearly dead and starting to get going or her zombie engine is rolling and the heroes are nearly unstoppable. &nbsp;She likes the risk reward of him. &nbsp;</p><p>Ra or Wraith are amazing with him since their return damage can kill the litle buggers.</p><p>Haka and Nighmist are also lots of fun with him.</p><p>Scholar as well, he's just ridiculous wth them.</p><p>AZ Using Thermal on them with only 1 villain target is awesome as well.</p><p>There's just so many ways to deal with them, and the effects get so good.</p><p>They are a lot of fun vs. the Ennead, Those silly thieves just keep killing them for you, esp. when you flip the one that destroys them for free.</p><p>I love the games with Necro, the increase in amount of shenanigans makes it so much fun.</p><p>He messes with the normal order of things, and I think that is a very good thing.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I like the theme, he is summoning the zombies to use for his magic which helps his allies, the Zombies don't fight for him, they are just there as spell components. &nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
