      {
        "id": 94398,
        "name": "PePe QuiCoSE",
        "username": "PePe_QuiCoSE",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/ecae2f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-04T00:33:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Necro's another one that leaves me cold.&nbsp; He summons minions which chew on the heroes, although he can do things with the minions which are helpful.&nbsp; Why not just skip the middle part with the chewing and have him summon minions that are helpful?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Beacuse it's not the same dynamic. It's good to have a different mechanic and a different feel for it. I do think Necro is a bit weak and can end up being not fun with so much setup and not that much payoff. [edit: I haven't played him as phanta has so I might be off. I still do not like when Heroes depend on other Heroes to be useful]</p>\n<p>In case of the Stranger, the damage works as a limit of how many Runes he can sustain per turn. I think it's good since it looks like it works.</p>\n<p>In general I like tosx cards better when it doesn't include any of the official Heroes/Villains (but it includes other of his own), it just feels more polished. The lack of bios also make them lacking in personality compared to official Heroes/Villains.</p>",
